{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419181-scion-atlantis-visuals","id":1419181,"title":"Scion Atlantis Visuals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-20T09:48:25-07:00","id":1419181,"title":"Scion Atlantis Visuals","content":"So I want to make the 'Atlantis Returns' chronicle with help of <b>Scion 2E Companion - Mysteries of the World (MotW)</b>. As there was great <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> (<b>MtAw</b>) book for making pulp 'temples' called <b>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</b> (<b>SoRT</b>), I extract stuff from this. In last book there is mentioned <b>Stargate SG-1</b> TV series as inspirations - and now I rewatch <b>SG-1</b>. Question - <b>How much <i>Stargate</i> ascetic works with Atlantean Pantheon from <i>MotW</i>? </b>Should Atlantis Realms look like this - or maybe other imaginary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T12:39:10-07:00","id":1419202,"title":"","content":"From how Atlantis in Mysteries of the World is described, I would go even further back than Stargate. Go for Impossibly Advanced but with designs that evoke an ancient aesthetic. Lots of crystals, shining clouds of nanotech in the workshop.<br /> <br /> And when all else fails, look at the Protoss from Starcraft. Lots of curved designs, elegant golden color scheme, gleaming crystals of immense power.<br /> <br /> Granted that's entirely from my brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T09:40:24-07:00","id":1419597,"title":"","content":"Going by Protoss idea by <b>Kyman</b>, I think about general themes and motifs of Atlantean Pantheon - like, that their whole myth tell that they come from black void. Instead on the island, I would put Theros on lonely 'land' ( planet? ) in great vacuum of space. As I plan Atlanteans to come back to Earth in my chronicle, they would be locked in some far space realm - something like Ancients spaceship <i>Destiny </i>in <b>Stargate: Universe</b> TV series. The whole 'Atlantis' would be colony that run away not on Earth - but to the deep stars. And now, they finally return to Earth...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -m